<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Friuli</h1><p class="st-meta">568 CE – 776 CE · capital Cividale del Friuli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Lombard duchy in Italy, a frontier march at Cividale guarding the north-eastern passes against Avars and Slavs.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombards">Lombards</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 568, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">King Alboin</a> left his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gisulf-i-of-friuli">Gisulf</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cividale-del-friuli">Forum Iulii</a> (Cividale del <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>) with chosen warrior families to hold the passes from the Julian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. It became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> duchy, and the name Friuli comes from Forum Iulii.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> were warrior frontier lords, often fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> to the east. In 610 the Avars sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cividale-del-friuli">Cividale</a> and killed Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gisulf-ii-of-friuli">Gisulf II</a>. The historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-the-deacon">Paul the Deacon</a> came from a Friulian family. Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratchis">Ratchis</a> became king in 744; the altar he commissioned and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tempietto-longobardo">Tempietto Longobardo</a> in Cividale are masterpieces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> art. The patriarchs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a> also resided at Cividale.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard Kingdom</a>, Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hrodgaud">Hrodgaud of Friuli</a> rebelled in 776 and was killed. Charlemagne replaced him with Frankish counts, and the territory became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/march-of-friuli">March of Friuli</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-friuli.jpg" alt="Duchy of Friuli" width="320" height="265"><figcaption>Image: Wario2 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lombard_(Kingdom_of)_Italy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>568 CE – 776 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cividale del Friuli</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gisulf I, Ratchis, Hrodgaud</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombardic, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>, <a href="/countries/slovenia">Slovenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lombard Duchy of Friuli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=672&amp;focus=duchy-of-friuli" aria-label="Duchy of Friuli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4997 555 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Friuli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5317 811L5218 839M5317 811L5139 672M5317 811L5308 809"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 839h0M5139 672h0M5308 809h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5317 811h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5317 811h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cividale del Friuli. <a href="/atlas?year=672&amp;focus=duchy-of-friuli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
